    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling day against a slate of vulnerable arms, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (75.38) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, benefiting from a soft matchup against Nick Martinez, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is the clear beneficiary of a high-leverage spot against Spence (6.03 xERA). Spence is arguably the most favorable target on the board today, and we have leaned heavily into that matchup by starting **Curtis Mead** (63.58) and the high-speed **Nasim Nunez** (62.09). Despite **Nasim Nunez** batting ninth, his raw efficiency against a weak SP_xERA makes him a strong start, particularly given our aggressive focus on stolen base potential.\n\nOur most critical lineup decisions were centered around the outfield and utility spots, where **Andy Pages** (69.52) and **Jackson Merrill** (65.84) surged into starting roles. **Andy Pages** earns a slight edge over the rest of the pack due to the park environment and a favorable platoon setup against Martinez. The most difficult benching decision involved **Cole Carrigg**, who just missed the \"Strong\" start threshold with a 58.50 score; while his switch-hitting ability and wind advantage against Imanaga provided a boost, the high strikeout threat posed by the left-handed Imanaga relegated **Cole Carrigg** to the bench to preserve our game cap. \n\nRegarding risks, we are closely monitoring **Liam Hicks**, who sits at 45.31; facing an elite arm like Wheeler (3.16 xERA) significantly caps his upside despite the leadoff spot. We have no concerns regarding the availability of our stars, as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** are merely resting due to scheduled team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently occupying IL slots, our depth remains tested, but the current configuration is optimized to maximize run production and stolen base opportunities against a shaky crop of starters.",
